      "message": "This currently waits for 5s. Can you either:\na) significantly shorten the timeout (you\u0027ll have to play around a little bit, but I think about 50ms should probably be plenty -- though I don\u0027t know how it affects other tests (if some request a tethered interface without waiting for the interface to be available in EthernetTracker, this may not work)) or\nb) add a second getInterface() method that takes the timeout?\n\nIf you do that, I suggest to just run this before every test. The added complexity of having to initialize context, EthernetManager, and TetheredInterfaceRequester is not worth it to save less than half a second. (4 tests wait on timeout, so even if you find you have to set it to 500ms (which I doubt), it should still be an acceptable price to pay.)",
